Level 9 → Level 10

Concept
This file is mostly garbage/binary data, and the password is buried 
somewhere in it as one small chunk of actual readable text. Trying to 
cat or open it directly would just dump a wall of unreadable noise - 
this level is testing whether you know a tool built specifically for 
pulling human-readable text out of binary files.

Commands used
strings data.txt

## Why it works
strings scans through a file and pulls out any sequence of printable 
characters, ignoring everything else that isn't readable text. Since 
the file is mostly binary junk with the password sitting in there as 
plain text, strings filters out the noise and surfaces just the 
readable pieces - including the password - without needing to manually 
sift through raw binary data.
